# What this folder is, and what therefore does NOT belong in git
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything here is reproducible from two commands:
#
#   pip install -r requirements.txt
#   python run_all.py          # download -> extract -> train -> report -> ONNX
#
# so this file ignores the artefacts those produce and keeps what a reader
# actually has to review: the code, the settings, the trained weights (80 KB
# each, so `app.py` runs on a fresh clone without retraining), and the small
# written reports.  Without these rules the folder offers git 698 files and
# 116 MB; with them it is ~50 files under 2 MB.

# ------------------------------------------------------------- generated data
# cache/ is the extracted landmark store: 629 files, 76 MB, and 622 of those
# files are one-per-clip MSL trajectories.  Rebuilt by
#   python src/extract_landmarks.py            (~20 min, 12 workers)
#   python src/extract_msl_landmarks.py  --    (only if the MSL clips are back)
cache/

# KaggleHub stores dataset downloads here. The images are local training data
# and must never be committed.
datasets/
data/raw/
*.7z
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi

# MediaPipe's own hand model (7.5 MB) is *downloaded* by src/download_data.py,
# and app.py's self-healing path checks for it at runtime.
models/hand_landmarker.task

# ------------------------------------------------------------- big evidence
# reports/*.csv dumps are per-frame: reports/oof_all.csv alone is 23 MB and
# 122,359 rows.  Regenerate with
#   python src/train.py --profile all --dump-preds reports/oof_all.csv
# The .md reports and the confusion-matrix PNGs stay in - they are the argument.
reports/oof_*.csv
reports/preds_*.csv
reports/samples/
*.parquet
*.parquet.tmp
*.npz
*.pkl

# ------------------------------------------------------- python / tool noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Run logs: useful on the machine that ran them, noise in a diff.
*.log
train_log.txt
extract_log.txt

# Scratch / editor / OS leftovers, incl. the temp files this project writes
# next to its parquet before renaming them into place.
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*~
~$*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# Never commit a Kaggle token or a Streamlit secret.  `download_data.py` reads
# ~/.kaggle/kaggle.json on purpose so that there is no reason to put one here.
.env
.env.*
kaggle.json
.secrets/
kaggle_token.txt
access_token
access_token.txt
credentials.json
.streamlit/secrets.toml
